From e5229733e33ceb0381984cab355a3d49fb367a76 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 17:10:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] j604: report the speaker graph's latency

The J604 speaker graph delays the sound by 1388 samples (28.9 ms) on the
tweeters and 1868 samples (38.9 ms) on the woofers at 48 kHz, and reports
0 to PipeWire, so every player plays the sound that much after the picture
it aimed it at.

Measured offline with this graph's controls and lsp-plugins-lv2 1.2.37
(a click through each plugin, at 256, 1024 and 2048 frame blocks, all the
same): the two loudness compensators (fft 2) 1024 samples each, the band
compressor and the compressor on the woofers 240 each (their 5 ms
sidechain look-ahead), the two limiters 364 each (5 ms look-ahead plus
the oversampler). The IRs are minimum phase (peaks at sample 0 and 33).

PipeWire's filter graph sums its nodes' latency once, right after
activate() and before the first run(), when the LSP plugins still report
0; the loudness compensator would then report 7680 samples, not the 1024
it delays. A file IR counts as 0. So the graph reports 0 whatever the
plugins do.

Give every convolver a "latency" equal to the TWEETER path's delay at
48 kHz. PipeWire's filter graph publishes the midpoint of its shortest
and longest output paths, so declaring the woofers' real 38.9 ms would
make it report 33.9 ms and put the tweeters, which carry speech, 5 ms
ahead of the picture. With one value on all four the graph is aligned,
reports 1388 samples (28.9 ms), and players put the tweeters on the
picture; the woofers stay 10 ms behind them, as they already are in
the graph. The sound is unchanged.

The value is exact at 48 kHz; at 44.1 kHz the graph delays 2.1 ms more
than it reports, at 88.2 and 96 kHz about 11 ms less, because part of the
delay is fixed in samples and part in milliseconds.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 firs/j604/graph.json | 12 ++++++++----
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/firs/j604/graph.json b/firs/j604/graph.json
index 3e84625..92a831d 100644
--- a/firs/j604/graph.json
+++ b/firs/j604/graph.json
@@ -50,7 +50,8 @@
                         "/usr/share/asahi-audio/j314/tweeters-192.wav"
                     ],
                     "channel": 0,
-                    "gain": 1.0
+                    "gain": 1.0,
+                    "latency": 0.0289167
                 }
             },
             {
@@ -65,7 +66,8 @@
                         "/usr/share/asahi-audio/j314/tweeters-192.wav"
                     ],
                     "channel": 0,
-                    "gain": 1.0
+                    "gain": 1.0,
+                    "latency": 0.0289167
                 }
             },
